---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Locations', url: '/locations/' },
  { name: 'Bible Study Fourways', url: '/bible-study-fourways/' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Is there a Bible study group in Fourways?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. Johannesburg Bible Study Church serves Fourways and the surrounding suburbs of Lonehill, Beverley, Craigavon, Sunninghill, and Bryanston. Our main programme is a free Wednesday evening online Bible study that anyone from Fourways can join via Google Meet.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Where do Fourways residents meet for Bible study?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Most Fourways residents who attend our Bible study join the Wednesday online session at 7:30pm from home. For in-person meetings, our main community hub is at Parkmore, 11th Street, Sandton — about 15 to 25 minutes drive from most Fourways suburbs, depending on traffic.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Is the Fourways Bible study free?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. Our Bible study is free. The Sunday Korean class has a course fee. Please contact us for current Korean class fees.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What time does the Bible study meet?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Wednesday evenings, 7:30pm to 9:00pm, online via Google Meet. You can log in from home. The in-person Saturday Bible study in Parkmore is once a month, first Saturday of the month, 4:00pm to 5:30pm.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Bible Study in Fourways | Wednesday Group for Fourways Residents"
  description="Looking for a Bible study in Fourways, Johannesburg? Free Wednesday evening group for Fourways, Lonehill, Beverley, Sunninghill and Bryanston residents. Online via Google Meet. All welcome."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-max max-w-4xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-blue-600 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Bible Study in Fourways</p>
      <h1 class="heading-1 mb-6">Bible Study in Fourways: A Free Wednesday Group for Residents of Fourways, Lonehill, Beverley and Bryanston</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-8">
        If you searched <em>bible study fourways</em>, you are probably somewhere between "I should really find a church" and "I just need one good conversation with someone who takes this seriously". Both are good reasons to be here.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10">
        <p class="font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-3">This page covers:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-blue-900 text-sm">
          <li>✓ What our Wednesday evening group is honestly like</li>
          <li>✓ The Fourways suburbs we serve most</li>
          <li>✓ How to join in three simple steps</li>
          <li>✓ Driving directions from major Fourways suburbs to Parkmore</li>
          <li>✓ Frequently asked questions specific to Fourways residents</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">Why Fourways Is on Our Radar</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        Fourways is one of the fastest-growing parts of northern Johannesburg. New families are moving in all the time, often from elsewhere in South Africa or from abroad. Lonehill, Beverley, Craigavon, Sunninghill, and the new builds around Waterfall are full of people looking for community. Many of them are looking for a Bible study that is not stuffy, not performative, and not Sunday-morning-only.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        That is exactly what we have been trying to build for ten years. Our Wednesday evening online group is the centre of it. People join from their homes after the kids are in bed, from their studies, or even from the lounge after a braai. It is the easiest way for Fourways residents to find a serious Bible study without driving anywhere on a work night.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">The Wednesday Evening Bible Study</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        Wednesdays, 7:30pm to 9:00pm, on Google Meet. We open in prayer, read a passage, and discuss. The group has about a dozen to two dozen regulars from across Johannesburg — Sandton, Randburg, Roodepoort, Soweto, Fourways, Midrand, and Centurion.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        The Bible study is unhurried. We take four to five weeks on each chapter, and we ask slow questions like "what did you notice", "what did you disagree with", "what would this look like on a Tuesday morning in Lonehill". Scepticism is welcome. There is no test, no quiz, no expectation of prior knowledge.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">Who Joins from Fourways</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        We have a steady contingent from Fourways proper, plus regulars from Lonehill, Beverley, Sunninghill, Craigavon, and the edges of Bryanston. A few drive in from the new estates around Waterfall and from Kyalami, which is technically Midrand but right on the border.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        The Fourways crowd is the youngest slice of our community. Many are in their late twenties to early forties, with young kids. Several are first-time Bible study attendees who came along because a friend invited them and stayed because they liked the tone. About a third of the Fourways group are not from a Christian background — they came out of curiosity and have stayed for the community.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">In-Person Options in Parkmore</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        For Fourways residents who want to meet in person, our main hub is at Parkmore, 11th Street, Sandton. Off-peak driving time is 15 to 20 minutes from most Fourways suburbs. Peak traffic can stretch it to 30 to 40 minutes, which is why most of our Fourways members prefer the Wednesday online session.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        Two in-person programmes happen at Parkmore:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 mb-6 list-disc pl-6 text-body">
        <li><strong>Korean Class</strong> — Sundays at 3:00pm. About 90 minutes. Beginners welcome. A course fee applies.</li>
        <li><strong>First Saturday In-Person Bible Study</strong> — once a month, first Saturday, 4:00pm. Smaller, more conversational than the Wednesday group.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">UseCan Youth Programme for Fourways Teens</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        Our youth programme, UseCan, runs on Saturdays at 3:00pm in Parkmore. It is open to teenagers aged 13 to 18 from anywhere in Johannesburg — we have a number of Fourways, Lonehill, and Bryanston teens in the programme. The drive is about 20 minutes from Lonehill, 25 from Beverley. The cost is free.
      </p>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">How to Join</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-3 mb-6 list-decimal pl-6 text-body">
        <li>Call or WhatsApp <strong>Mr. Sim on +27 77 487 1295</strong> or <strong>Ms. Dora on +27 67 442 4461</strong>.</li>
        <li>We send you the Google Meet link the morning of the session.</li>
        <li>Log in at 7:30pm. Camera on or off. Pyjamas welcome.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">Driving Directions from Major Fourways Suburbs</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 mb-6 list-disc pl-6 text-body">
        <li><strong>From Fourways Mall area:</strong> William Nicol north, turn onto Jan Smuts, into Sandton. About 20 minutes off-peak.</li>
        <li><strong>From Lonehill:</strong> Main Road to Lonehill Boulevard, onto William Nicol, into Sandton. About 18 minutes off-peak.</li>
        <li><strong>From Beverley or Craigavon:</strong> Main Road to William Nicol. About 22 minutes off-peak.</li>
        <li><strong>From Sunninghill:</strong> Sunninghill Drive onto N1 south, William Nicol off-ramp. About 25 minutes off-peak.</li>
        <li><strong>From Bryanston:</strong> Main Road into Sandton via Katherine. About 15 minutes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <details class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Do you have a Sunday service in Fourways?</summary>
          <p class="text-body mt-3">No. We do not run a traditional Sunday service in Fourways. Our in-person hub is in Parkmore, Sandton. If you are looking for a Sunday service close to Fourways, we can recommend a few — call us.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Is there a Bible study specifically for young adults?</summary>
          <p class="text-body mt-3">Our Wednesday group skews young adult, with most regulars in their late twenties to early forties. There is no separate "young adults" track, but the tone of the group tends to fit that demographic well.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Can my teenager attend UseCan from Fourways?</summary>
          <p class="text-body mt-3">Yes. UseCan meets in Parkmore on Saturdays at 3:00pm. The drive is about 20 minutes from most Fourways suburbs. Many Fourways families are part of the programme.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">I am from another country. Will I fit in?</summary>
          <p class="text-body mt-3">Yes. About a third of our regulars are not South African. We have regulars from the UK, Zimbabwe, Nigeria, India, Korea, the US, and elsewhere. The Wednesday group has a relaxed, international feel.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Is there parking at Parkmore?</summary>
          <p class="text-body mt-3">Yes. The Parkmore Community Room has safe off-street parking. Sandton is a busy area on weekdays but the community room is easy to access.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <h2 class="heading-2 mb-4 mt-10">The Honest Bottom Line</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6">
        Fourways is full of people who have moved here recently and are quietly looking for community. Our Wednesday online Bible study is built for exactly that kind of person — serious about the Bible, not interested in performance, free, and easy to try. Phone numbers: <strong>Mr. Sim +27 77 487 1295</strong>, <strong>Ms. Dora +27 67 442 4461</strong>. One sentence is enough.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-blue-100 border border-blue-300 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10 mt-10">
        <p class="font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-3">Related pages:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-blue-900 text-sm">
          <li>→ <a href="/free-bible-study-sandton/" class="underline">Free Bible Study in Sandton</a></li>
          <li>→ <a href="/online-bible-study-johannesburg/" class="underline">Online Bible Study in Johannesburg</a></li>
          <li>→ <a href="/bible-study-randburg/" class="underline">Bible Study in Randburg</a></li>
          <li>→ <a href="/locations/fourways/" class="underline">Fourways Location Overview</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>